## 🏛️ Maat Order: Rational Kernels vs Trash

**Maat Order = Keep what works (rational kernels) + Discard what doesn't (trash) + Evidence (prove)**

### Rational Kernels (Keep - Evidence-Based)
- ✅ gitMaat system (coordinates all projects)
- ✅ TehutiGuard protection (enforces three-ring)
- ✅ Memory Bank documentation (clear structure)
- ✅ Project discovery (auto-setup works)
- ✅ AGENTS.md system (agents read successfully)

### Trash (Discard - Evidence-Based)
- ❌ System prompt too narrow (doesn't understand ecosystem)
- ❌ OpenCode no Maat integration (can't coordinate)
- ❌ Confusion about tools (not clearly defined)
- ❌ No evidence-based decisions (can't prove what works)

**See**: `docs/MAAT-ORDER-AUDIT.md` for complete assessment.

